          'Furthermore, commercial ice machines operate with 115V or 208/230V electrical circuits powering high-voltage compressors, condenser fan motors, and water circulation pumps. Water pooling near electrical conduits, base receptacles, or cord drops presents an immediate electrocution and equipment short-circuit hazard.',
