          'Air-Cooled Condensers are the most popular and cost-effective commercial units. They pull ambient air through a radiator fin coil and discharge hot air into the room. In well-ventilated kitchens or back-of-house storage corridors, air-cooled units deliver the lowest lifetime operating cost. However, in small, enclosed rooms with inadequate HVAC, air-cooled units overheat, triggering high-head-pressure safeties that trip compressors.',
